- DIPLOMACY: improving NPC attitude by one step requires a Diplomacy check. DC depends on current
  attitude: hostile DC 25+CHA mod, unfriendly DC 20+CHA mod, indifferent DC 15+CHA mod, friendly
  DC 10+CHA mod. Shifting two steps in one check increases DC by 10. Takes 1 minute of
  conversation (cannot rush in most cases).
- INTIMIDATE: demoralize in combat is a standard action vs DC 10+HD+WIS mod. Out of combat,
  forcing cooperation uses the same skill but the effect is temporary and the NPC becomes
  unfriendly afterward.
- BLUFF AND SENSE MOTIVE: opposed checks. Bluff DC modifiers: +0 believable, +5 unlikely,
  +10 far-fetched, +20 impossible. Sense Motive can also detect enchantment (DC 25).
- ATTITUDE TRACKING: note any attitude shifts in consequences so the context update step can
  track NPC dispositions accurately.
- GATHER INFORMATION: This is a use of the DIPLOMACY skill, NOT a standalone skill called
  "Gather Information". Always request a Diplomacy check (skill: "Diplomacy"). Gathering
  information in a settlement takes 1d4 hours. DC 10 for common knowledge, DC 20+ for
  obscure or protected information.
